[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) says one issue, one fix queued. Read the reports and it is three. The
merge rule ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)) matched on subject, and every
report about a wrong date has a subject that sounds the same.

<Callout kind="warn">
#4471 was closed on 5 Oct, but its problems were not fixed. The parser fix covers EU locales only,
and <code>en-GB</code> is not one. The hint stays on booking-v3, which three tenants still run. The one-day
move was never in the update. Details are under <em>After the 5 Oct engineering update</em>.
</Callout>

## What is in #4471

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {issues} />

Counted the desk's way, from the export as it is: each id once (the export repeats some reports
across its pages), each report under the cause it is filed by tenant. *Mistagged* counts the
reports intake tagged as something else: intake guesses from the reporter's browser, the cause
depends on the tenant.

## The three problems

**`parser`: the shared parser reads dates month first.** Day-first tenants get day and month
swapped: "Our 7 April reminder went out on 4 July." Every tenant on file, every channel. This is the
fix #4471 had queued; what shipped covers EU locales only.

**`hint`: booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field.** People at day-first tenants type
what the hint says, month first, and the form reads it the tenant's way. Same swap, different bug:
only reports through the form, only tenants on booking-v3. Fixing the parser does not touch it; the
hint has to follow the tenant's locale.

**`one-day`: the date moves by exactly one day.** "Invite says Tuesday 12 May. Calendar says Monday
11 May." "Client in Lisbon got Tuesday. Client in Toronto got Monday. Same meeting." No month or day
is swapped, so neither fix above reaches it. It reads like a timezone conversion on the date. The
desk already noted these (`desk-notes.json`) and files them under `parser` by tenant, so they
count in both rows.

## After the 5 Oct engineering update

Engineering closed #4471 on 5 Oct: `parser` fixed ("fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales"),
`hint` won't fix ("booking-v3 form retired"). Checked against the export and the tenant directory,
closing it leaves all three problems open:

<UpdateCheck ticket={4471} {issues} />

- **`parser`:** the fix covers EU locales only. harbour.dental writes dates in `en-GB`, and the UK is
  not in the EU. Its reports run up to 4 Oct, the day before the close. The parser has to read
  every day-first locale, not a list of EU ones.
- **`hint`:** the tenant directory still lists three tenants on booking-v3. Until they are moved
  off it, the form is not retired for them, and its hint still says `MM/DD/YYYY`.
- **`one-day`:** the update does not mention it. Closing #4471 drops it.

## For the desk

- When a report gives both dates, check them: a swap and a one-day move are not the same bug.
- Place a report by its tenant and channel, not by the intake tag.
- Reopen #4471 as the `parser` ticket only, until the parser reads every day-first locale; the
  other two have their own.
- Check whether a "retired" form is still listed for a tenant before closing a ticket on it.

